2026-10-26 | Event and incident-particle energy records
- User-requested baseline checkpoint completed first: 1c77a24 (LMO sensitive detector and explicit LMO naming).
- Add top-level DetectorHit and change LMOSD/Edep from G4THitsMap<double> totals to DetectorHitsCollection with per-detector, per-track deposits, including zero-deposit visits and unhit detectors. Keep SD beside Actions; no physics or geometry changes.
- Add record/EnergyRecord, EventEnergyRecorder, IncidentEnergyRecorder and TrackAncestry. Record classes consume event-owned hit collections; incident roots are resolved separately for each detector using parent IDs and birth volumes, with cached iterative traversal, error detection and unique energy ownership.
- Wire EventAction and TrackingAction through ActionInitialization: event-local ancestry includes every tracked particle; event end creates both record vectors; next event clears state and aborted events produce no result rows. SD names come from constructed LMO volumes.
- User-confirmed policy: each detector has its own incident roots; descendants born there inherit the root, crossings into another detector start that detector's branch, in-detector primaries root at themselves, and re-entry of the same track is merged. A parent that never visited the target detector cannot establish a branch there.
- Reference review: LMO-Th232-sim/analyse/EnergyReconstruction.C recursively sums descendant tracks for each externally born candidate; separate roots in the same subtree can overlap. New recording assigns every detector/track deposit to exactly one root and preserves zero-deposit ancestors.
- API verification: official Geant4 11.4 tracking/hit documentation and local 11.4.1 tracking initialization, G4HCofThisEvent and G4THitsCollection sources. No ROOT output or extra output fields added in this step.
- Validation: targeted ancestry tests, real serial/MT transport and regression checks pending.
- Add deterministic energy-record tests for genealogy attribution, cross-detector roots, zero-deposit ancestors, internal primaries, outside-born re-entry branches, no-visit-parent fallback, generic LD/NTD names, 20000-track chains, invalid/missing ancestry, event reset and abortion. Extend real SD transport tests to execute production EventAction/TrackingAction and compare both record totals against an independent step sum for electrons, external gammas, through-going muons and geantinos in serial/MT runs.
- Build adjustment: G4String has no default std::hash specialization in this installation; use std::set for the small detector-name uniqueness checks. Integer ancestry caches remain unordered maps.
- Validation adjustment: the standalone record test must register a minimal Geant4 physics list before constructing EventAction; corrected the test setup after Geant4 rejected early Action construction. All six real transport record tests already passed. README now documents schemas, per-detector ancestry policy, zero rows, lifetime, output integration and deferred metadata.
- Final validation: Geant4 11.4.1 Release build and link passed. All 13 CTest cases passed in 63.62 seconds, including deterministic genealogy/error/lifecycle tests, a 20000-track chain, and six serial/two-worker integration cases with 72 events each (432 total across consecutive runs). Real secondary deposits were confirmed; event totals and sums of incident-root totals matched independent per-step accumulation. Existing materials, geometry/macros, generators, samplers and decay/transport smoke tests passed. git diff --check passed. Current results are in-memory records only; no ROOT or experimental spectrum validation claimed. New record changes remain uncommitted after baseline 1c77a24.


